From: Lume Retro OS
Subject: [PATCH] gfx_widgets: LUME_HUD, LUME_HINT and LUME_MENU over the game

lume-run owns the status bar, the chord hint and the Lume menu over a game
(lume-hud-actions D8, D10, D13) but cannot draw while RetroArch owns the
screen. Three network commands draw what lume-run sends, as graphics widgets
(gfx_widget_lume, kept in gfx_widget_volume.c so the build files do not
change, like 0011):

  LUME_HUD  <group|group|...>       a strip along the top, semi-transparent,
                                    the game's viewport untouched; the first
                                    word of each group (the label) in the
                                    accent, a thin divider between groups
  LUME_HINT <button\tname|...>      a centred panel, one row per Fn chord
  LUME_MENU <title|item|...|focus>  the Lume menu: the game dimmed, a panel
                                    with a title and the focused row filled

RetroArch interprets nothing: "-" (or no text) hides a widget, and each one
hides by itself 3 s after its last command, so a dead lume-run leaves nothing
on the screen. Nothing pauses the game here; lume-run pauses it for the menu
(GET_STATUS + PAUSE_TOGGLE). LUME_MENU is the reserve path of D14 while the
system-drawn menu waits for its proof on the consoles. The command channel
listens on 127.0.0.1 only (patch 0009).

diff --git a/command.c b/command.c
index 6a9b40f..5d0f63e 100644
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -756,6 +756,37 @@ bool command_lume_level(command_t *cmd, const char* arg)
    return true;
 }
 
+/* Lume: the status bar, the chord hint and the Lume menu over the game, sent
+ * by lume-run (lume-hud-actions D8). RetroArch only draws the text it gets;
+ * "-" (or nothing) hides the widget, and each one hides by itself 3 s after
+ * the last command. */
+bool command_lume_hud(command_t *cmd, const char* arg)
+{
+#if defined(HAVE_GFX_WIDGETS)
+   if (gfx_widgets_ready())
+      gfx_widget_lume_show(GFX_WIDGET_LUME_HUD, arg);
+#endif
+   return true;
+}
+
+bool command_lume_hint(command_t *cmd, const char* arg)
+{
+#if defined(HAVE_GFX_WIDGETS)
+   if (gfx_widgets_ready())
+      gfx_widget_lume_show(GFX_WIDGET_LUME_HINT, arg);
+#endif
+   return true;
+}
+
+bool command_lume_menu(command_t *cmd, const char* arg)
+{
+#if defined(HAVE_GFX_WIDGETS)
+   if (gfx_widgets_ready())
+      gfx_widget_lume_show(GFX_WIDGET_LUME_MENU, arg);
+#endif
+   return true;
+}
+
 
 bool command_load_state_slot(command_t *cmd, const char *arg)
 {
